00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.840
the table." – National Security Council&nbsp;
spokesperson in remarks to the WSJ).
 &nbsp;

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:59.460
In other words, Iran needed to find new partners.&nbsp;
And Visualpolitik viewers, this is exactly where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.700
today’s great protagonist enters the scene.
 
Pay close attention.&nbsp;

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:11.160
WHAT IS CHINA DOING IN THE MIDDLE EAST?)
 &nbsp;

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.960
China's presence in the Middle East and North&nbsp;
Africa is not strictly new. In 1956 it had already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.920
succeeded in making Egypt the first country in the&nbsp;
region to recognize the People's Republic of China&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:27.300
as the real China to the detriment of Taiwan.
 
However, since the arrival of Xi Jinping,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.020
the stakes have become much clearer,&nbsp;
especially with regard to Iran.
 &nbsp;

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:34.920
(China and Iran seal partnership&nbsp;
with 25-year cooperation pact&nbsp;

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.640
Although no details have emerged,&nbsp;
the pact broadly envisages Chinese&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:42.780
investments of around $400 billion in the&nbsp;
Iranian energy sector. – El Confidencial)
 &nbsp;

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:45.840
However, if we compare them with the&nbsp;
relations that China has forged with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.740
Saudi Arabia over recent decades,&nbsp;
Iran seems to be on a second level.
 &nbsp;

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.680
After Deng Xiaoping came to power and&nbsp;
opened up to the rest of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:56.760
the Asian giant's economy took off. And do you&nbsp;
know what that means? That China needed more and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:01.920
more oil. And where is the most secure and stable&nbsp;
supply of crude oil? Exactly in Saudi Arabia.
 &nbsp;

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:05.220
In this way, the Saudis&nbsp;
became Beijing's key supplier.&nbsp;

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.900
In 2022, Russia snatched the top spot from Saudi&nbsp;
Arabia, but you all know why that happened.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:12.960
Be that as it may, the fact is that in&nbsp;
recent years China has been strengthening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.400
its relations with both Iran and Saudi Arabia.
 
And that's exactly what explains how Beijing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:21.420
managed to finalise a deal for these two great&nbsp;
enemies to shake hands again. As you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:25.380
a fat check can always work miracles.
 
Of course, in addition to the money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.600
the timing was also right.
 
Listen up.&nbsp;

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.600
GAME CHANGES)
 &nbsp;

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:42.060
After seven years of enormous tension&nbsp;
between Riyadh and Tehran, on 10 March&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:46.380
2023 both countries decided to shake hands. At&nbsp;
least to restore their diplomatic relations.
 &nbsp;

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:50.340
And let's see, I think we can all understand that&nbsp;
when your main client asks you for something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:55.260
you are at least receptive. In a way, that's what&nbsp;
has happened between Saudi Arabia and China.
 &nbsp;

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:59.820
This time, however, dollars are not the only&nbsp;
reason. After all, China needs Saudi Arabia more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:03.720
than the Arab country needs the Asian giant. If&nbsp;
China were to reduce its purchases of crude oil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:07.440
the Saudis could easily place that oil on the&nbsp;
international market. Remember that we are talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.820
about the country with the lowest extraction costs&nbsp;
on the planet, which means it has a higher margin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:15.720
than the rest of the dinosaur juice producers.
 
So this time, besides saving face with a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.380
client, Riyadh had three other good&nbsp;
reasons to shake hands with Tehran.&nbsp;

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:27.660
First of all, Saudi Arabia's relations with the&nbsp;
United States are not at their best and, in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:31.740
in Riyadh they are beginning to be wary of&nbsp;
the supposed American protection. In 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:35.520
for example, they suffered an attack by two&nbsp;
Iranian drones against their oil infrastructure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:39.120
without Washington lifting a finger. And&nbsp;
that happened with Trump in the White House,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:43.800
because now with Biden relations are even worse.
 
Secondly, the breakup in 2018 of the Joint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:47.460
Comprehensive Plan of Action that monitored&nbsp;
the Iranian nuclear program got on the nerves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.580
of the Saudi government, particularly due&nbsp;
to the lack of alternatives. In Riyadh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.580
they are terrified that Tehran could&nbsp;
succeed any day in getting hold of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:56.760
nuclear bomb... And that is why they hope&nbsp;
that China can curb these aspirations.
 &nbsp;

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.540
Finally, Iran has pledged to eliminate its&nbsp;
support for Yemen's Houthis, which will allow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:04.920
Saudi Arabia to reduce tension in a long-running&nbsp;
conflict that has now spanned nearly a decade.
 &nbsp;

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:12.120
Well, that's as far as Saudi Arabia is&nbsp;
concerned. For its part, Iran has its own goals:&nbsp;

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.540
Firstly, to reduce US influence in the region,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:21.420
which includes seeking escape routes&nbsp;
from international sanctions.
 &nbsp;

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:25.740
Secondly, to stop the development of the Abraham&nbsp;
agreements between Israel and the Arab countries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:29.400
You already know that Israel is the other&nbsp;
great enemy of Iran's Islamic revolution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:34.680
so Iran does not want under any circumstances that&nbsp;
Riyadh follows in the footsteps of Abu Dhabi and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:38.700
normalizes its relations with the Hebrew state.
And finally, they hope that with this agreement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:42.660
the risk of a military clash will dissipate.&nbsp;
Iran already has enough open fronts.
 &nbsp;

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:47.220
But what about China, and why is it so interested&nbsp;
in an issue like this? Quite simply: it is part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:51.780
of Xi Jinping's new strategy to present itself as&nbsp;
an influential player at the international level.
 &nbsp;

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:54.480
Let's not kid ourselves, the group&nbsp;
photograph of the representatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.280
of these three countries has been one of China's&nbsp;
greatest diplomatic successes in recent decades.
 &nbsp;

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:03.900
And, of course, this agreement also calms tensions&nbsp;
in a key region for China's energy supply. Keep in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:07.920
mind that 40-50% of all China's energy imports&nbsp;
come from the Middle East. And take note,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.280
because the United States buys fewer&nbsp;
than 1 million barrels/day from this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.760
region of the world, which is equivalent&nbsp;
to less than 5% of its total consumption.
 &nbsp;

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:18.300
In other words, a potential conflict in the Middle&nbsp;
East may be unimportant for the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:22.320
but it would be a nightmare for China.
 
Now, speaking of the United States, what does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:25.980
Washington think of this agreement? Many analysts&nbsp;
have suggested that it represents the end of US&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:30.180
influence in this region of the world. Some even&nbsp;
say that it has been a great diplomatic failure.
 &nbsp;

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:39.360
But is it really so? Well, let's see.
ALIVE AND KICKING)
 &nbsp;

